WEBVTT

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.900
Good morning, Head Discliplinarian!

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.110
Good morning, Manaka.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.450
Paprika Academy rule #84:

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.120
Always walk on the right side of the hallway.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.340
I'm sure you've been following that rule.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.020
Of course!

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.120
No problem!

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.620
Hmm.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.620
Class 1-C, Toudou Shion.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.710
Paprika Academy rule #61:

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.790
Walking while reading a book is not allowed.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:33.300
Worry not. For someone as amazing as myself,
walking while reading a book is a simple matter.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.260
Rules are rules! Here's your warning ticket.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.050
Don't need it.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.760
If that was a valid excuse we wouldn't need <i>me</i>.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.370
Come on, take it already!

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.770
I said I don't need it.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.730
Take it! Just take it!

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:54.200
That won't work. I can see your next ten moves clear as day!

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.740
We'll see about that...

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.040
Too easy!

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.040
Paprika Academy rule #84:

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.840
Always walk on the right side of the hallway.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.270
What is a disciplinarian doing breaking the rules?

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.390
I never thought I'd be handing myself a ticket...

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:30.570
I'm certain you haven't forgotten Dressing Pafé's declaration of war from yesterday.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.110
I suppose I haven't.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:36.030
We're having a one-on-one battle against SoLaMi SMILE today.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.910
Needless to say, Dressing Pafé will be the winner!

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.630
Hmm? You certainly sound confident.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.620
You'll find we're not that easy to beat.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.830
Really?

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.290
Time to get serious.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.760
I read ahead and saw Dressing Pafés victory. Go champion's word. No going back.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.340
My results come out as a SoLaMi SMILE victory.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.470
The numbers don't lie.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.750
That's interesting.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:06.280
Will the game plan prevail,
or the calculations?

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.520
Very well.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.940
Wow, this got really out of hand.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.830
Melon bread! Raisin toast! Baked noodles on the bread!

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:53.180
I'm really hungry. I need melon bread.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.840
I'm buying lunch all on my own today.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.800
Melon bread, please!

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.460
Make an order...

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.130
Pshu...

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.970
One melon bread, please.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.630
We're all sold out of those.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:12.670
Huh? Well, how about fruit custard or fried soy dough?

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:16.690
All of your favorites are already sold out today.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.400
Huh? No way...

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.910
Rice... Rice ball...

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.340
Lady Sophie, good luck on your first errand-chanko!

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:32.290
I really want to help out!

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.270
Wanting to help and being unable. The anxiety!

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:40.580
All I could get was a bean sprout sandwich...

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.290
Just as I predicted.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:48.720
My grand "Make the disciplinarian unable to buy her favorite bread" plan seems to have worked.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.640
Toudou Shion! Did you buy them all out?

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:53.430
Of course not.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:57.230
I simply showed this book to my classmates.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.450
Huh? A rakugo book?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.480
Allow me to explain!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.420
This rakugo book I showed around

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.830
was so funny that everyone who read it remembered something from it

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:08.170
and start laughing in the middle of class.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.550
And that laughter lead to a chain reaction,

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.330
interrupting the class.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.140
In his anger, the teacher made everyone run ten laps around the school.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:19.790
The students got tired from all the running and ended up craving sweet things.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:23.400
Consequently, all the sweet bread varieties were sold out.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.260
<i>That</i> was my plan.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:25.930
Huh?

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.510
How about it? Do you see the superiority of my predictive ability?

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.470
Not reallly. I actually like bean sprout sandwiches.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:34.270
Too bad for you.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.720
Um...

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.400
Sold out

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.980
Pshu...
Sold out

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:46.990
Lady Sophie, you couldn't make the purchase, but your stuggle was magnificent all the same.

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:54.790
Whoa, that book looks crazy hard.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:58.910
Rare to see you in the library, Manaka.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:01.920
Yeah, I'm on library duty this week,

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.300
so I have to take care of the class bookshelf.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.500
Well, I can help you find the right books.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.720
Oh, really? Yay!

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:14.970
Leave it to me. I'm known as the concierge of the school library.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:22.030
If books are what you need, I'm this library's one-woman universal consulting service.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:27.030
No thank you! We'll find the books in no time without your help.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:31.140
Poppycock! I could find them far more efficiently.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:32.910
I'm faster for sure.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:38.150
Very well! We'll have a competition.
The one who finds each book first wins.

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:41.380
Competition? Well, no way around it. I accept.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.300
Alright! Read the items on the list aloud.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.590
O-Okay!
Hurry up, Manaka.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.720
The Matcha Merchant Girl.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:56.100
There!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:59.210
That one is <i>The Macho Trenchant Girl</i>.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.550
Too easy.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.480
Damn you!

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.440
Pshu...

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.530
"Humans are ultimately solitary beings.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:18.830
These so-called "friends" are a malign influence that only leads to wasting of precious time."

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.630
Now these are words of wisdom after my heart!

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.340
I feel such sympathy for the author!

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.220
The next book is <i>The Red Dog</i>.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.300
There!

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.930
I got it first!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.430
No, I did!

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:37.850
Don't try this at home!★

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.180
Why thank you.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:39.930
Oh no you didn't!

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.150
<i>These shoes are...</i>

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:50.360
Seems she gave up!

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.150
Minami!

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:56.080
Why in the world is my Head Disciplinarian running in the library? Good heavens!

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.490
<i>Be quiet!</i> Don't make noise in the library!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:58.540
My apologies.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.290
I'm sorry. Please excuse me.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:03.250
And you're on the disciplinary committee and the other students look to you for...

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:07.460
And there goes my lunch break.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:13.180
Even I got into trouble for giving in to Toudou Shion's provocation... Don't forget this, me.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.680
Madam Disciplinarian!

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.810
I reign supreme both out here and in PriPara.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.890
And so no one may walk before me.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:21.680
That is all.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.730
Toudou! Running in the hallway is...

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.360
This is not running, merely brisk walking.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:35.280
But considering the layout of the building, and an estimate of the Headmistress's pace based on her height...

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:35.610
Right past there...

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.240
What are you mumb—

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:38.960
Oww!

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.580
And now you, Toudou? That's dangerous!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.920
Always look forward in the hallway! And no speedwalking!

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.420
Be careful and pay attention to your surroundings when moving!

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:48.710
Stop the speedwalking! No more speedwalking! It's dangerous!

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.880
I'm sorry. I'm very sorry.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.720
What did I tell you?

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:53.380
I'm sorry!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.220
You're so cool, Shion!

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.600
Are you headed to PriPara?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.430
Yesterday's show was fabulous!

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:05.940
I've been your fan since the go championships, but you're perfect as an idol too!

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:10.530
Thank you. And I'll be going all out today as well. Be there!

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.200
Madam Disciplinarian!

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.450
What? I'm in a hurry.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.950
Dressing Pafé will win today.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.240
I'm sorry to inform you, but according to my calculations,

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:31.130
there is a 99.9986% chance of an absolutely crushing SoLaMi SMILE victory.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.300
And my sense says the game is headed for an absolute Dressing Pafé victory.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.260
Make no mistake about it!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.720
Whose prediction will win out?

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.020
We're about to find out.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.360
PriPara Change Complete.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.370
Complete!

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.330
Complete-pri!

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.950
Pripara Change!

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.250
Finished!

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.170
Complete...

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:19.050
Alright! It's the moment you've been waiting for, PriPara fans!

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.100
Harvest Season: October Live!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.110
SoLaMi Smile!

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.570
Dressing Pafé!

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:30.130
Due to an appeal from both teams,

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:35.370
today is a special one-on-one between the hottest names in the Fledgling Idol bracket!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.160
This is going to be great!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:40.950
Sounds good to me!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.410
Let's start off by getting some initial thoughts from both teams!

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.190
Dressing Pafé just made a huge splash with their debut.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:50.370
What is your message to the world?

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:54.920
We vow to defeat SoLaMi SMILE!

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.850
So good luck to them!

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.840
That's some confidence.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:01.800
Yeah...

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:04.260
And we will, of course,

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.770
accept that challenge-pri!

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.190
We have quite the turn of events on our hands!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:14.700
The tension won't be leaving before the scores are announced!

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:21.110
Well... About done with the paperwork. Guess I'll head over to the stage.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.160
Hey.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:27.540
Klaus Henrik Poncetta Von Vogel Strobel Cash De La Manecca the Third.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.210
What is it?

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:34.750
Will Michel Georges Sandrelli Mezza Bonjour Francois Girgil Je T'aime the Fourth.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:39.470
I'll never forgive you for stealing Sophie-usa.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.470
However, don't underestimate me. Sophie was but one of my pawns.

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:47.770
Pawn? How dare you insult Sophie like that-kuma!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.230
Sophie's with us now-kuma!

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.940
Hmph! Keep shouting into the wind-usa.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:57.270
Dressing Pafé's show today will blow away all your yearnings for hibernation.

00:11:57.270 --> 00:12:00.190
Clean out your ears in preparation-usa.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:04.370
And now, who will go on stage first?

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:09.850
Speed is the essence of go, as it is for war.
I wish to get the first turn.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:12.330
We want the first turn too!

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:18.500
I don't really mind going second.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.920
Either is just as fun as the other.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:20.760
Yeah.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:27.100
They're showing that Studio BuriBuri movie on TV today, and that's going to steal all the viewers-pri.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:31.480
And the second slot will overlap with the movie, putting us at a disadvantage-pri!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.900
They've shown that before though, I really don't think...

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.230
Don't underestimate it-pri!

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:41.700
Well, seeing neither side is giving in, we'll decide with a fair match or rock-paper-scissors!

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.110
Fine by me-pri.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.200
Acknowledged.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.100
You better win, Shion!

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:49.950
Be it rock-paper-scissors or whatever, losing is not allowed!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.580
Do your best, Shion.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.620
Rock displays my steadfast determination!

00:12:55.620 --> 00:13:00.090
Mireille! I will start this game of rock-paper-scissors with rock!

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:04.440
Oh my! Shion has declared her choice ahead of time!

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:08.220
But who knows if she'll actually throw rock as she said?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.850
What to do? I really don't know-pri!

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:16.060
<i>She's trying to put pressure on me, but I won't fall for that-pri.</i>

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:19.480
Here we go! Contestants, establish eye contact.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.860
Rock, paper...

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:22.660
Scissors!

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:27.370
And they both go with Rock! It's a draw!

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.240
Tie, huh?

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.950
Incidentally. I intend to continue throwing rock.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.460
How about you?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.170
Whatever shall I do-pri?

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:40.880
<i>She's just saying that again? What a jerk.</i>

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.340
What are you gonna do?

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.550
How admirable-pri! You really live up to your reputation!

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:52.890
You actually threw rock like you said!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:56.230
Actually doing exactly what you said in a situation like this! That's so cool-pri!

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.850
So cool!

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.270
That's the Shion we know!

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.480
Keeping your word is so cool!

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.030
And then another rock!

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:09.410
<i>This should lower the chances of her using anything but rock.</i>

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.200
Ro, sham...

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.080
Bo!

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.450
It's paper!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.290
It's paper! Shion threw paper!

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:22.000
Not keeping true to your word-pri? I'm a bit disappointed-pri.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.630
Keep your wits about you!

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.010
Words aren't meant to hold people down.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.420
They set us free!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:29.390
She's so cool!

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:31.430
You're amazing too, Mireille!

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:35.640
<i>She's not just simple and straightforward. Tougher to deal with than expected.</i>

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.850
But the next round will be the last.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.900
I will no longer announce my choice!

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:45.070
A pure 50/50 chance! Let's plunge into the unknown!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.570
Just what I like to hear-pri!

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.240
Here we go then! Establish eye contact and...

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.240
Pri!

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:52.990
Go!

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.620
Uh, err...

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:02.040
That's the result!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:06.710
That's the move!

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:10.590
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:17.640
<i>To have matched my game sense... She's not bad.</i>

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:20.730
<i>How persistent can you get? I'm getting tired of this-pri...</i>

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.230
Oh my, we remain at standstill.

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:24.360
What do you say we move on to drawing straws...

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.440
Rock, paper, scissors! Ro, sham, bo!

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.650
Bo, bo, bobo, bo!

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:33.120
Bo, bo, bo, bo, bo, bo, bo, bo, bo!

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:34.830
All right! Victory!

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.080
I don't even care anymore.

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.790
Seriously...

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.460
You did it, Shion!

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.040
I'm just glad it's over.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.960
I ran out of stamina-pri.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.540
You did good, Mireille.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:49.510
So, we'll be making the first move.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:53.220
Go ahead-pri! We'll still win-pri!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.390
Let's beat that other program, Sophie!

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.270
Yeah.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.360
Scan the appropriate amount of My Tickets for your coord.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.310
You may also scan Friend Tickets.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:09.860
Coord Change Start!

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.340
The China Rock Dress.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:17.330
Can't beat the impact of the triple pandas.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:21.210
China Rock Dress, go.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.840
And behind every fluffy panda you can see the flash of cold hard metal chains.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:32.170
China Rock Honey Dress! Yay!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.930
Just "cute" isn't enough.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:38.350
The high boots give the outfits a hard finish.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.020
China Rock Forest Dress!

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.090
An idiosyncratic team with a rocking show: Start!

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.100
So cool! So powerful!

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.640
They've got endurance.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:32.480
Making Drama Switch On!

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:44.780
Stereo Full Blast Two-Three Rock!

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:50.690
Cyalume Change!

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.340
Go!

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.780
And continuing with SoLaMi SMILE's performance!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:17.450
Let's put on a show that won't let anyone change the channel. Blow that other show out of the water-pri!

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.200
Yeah!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.910
Full power!

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.540
Live! Let's go!

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:26.810
Pretty!

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.460
Paradise!

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.580
That's the way-kuma! Lookin' good-kuma!

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:07.840
I see. This overwhelming sense of joy.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:10.330
This is SoLaMi SMILE's appeal.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:15.920
Making Drama Switch On!

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:19.130
Someone save us!

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.080
Save us!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:29.850
Liberation Maiden Valkyria!

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:34.020
Cyalume Change!

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:40.450
Pri!

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:06.180
And now, both Dressing Pafé and SoLaMi SMILE have finished.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:12.140
Who got the most likes from our audience and the viewers at home?

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:15.560
Looks like a slight SoLaMi SMILE lead...

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:18.110
Now Dressing Pafé is going past them!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:21.530
It's a neck and neck struggle to the top.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:23.700
Who will emerge victorious?

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:27.200
Dressing Pafé with their stunning debut?

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:32.160
Or SoLaMi SMILE with their skyrocketing popularity after Houjou Sophie's inclusion?

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:36.920
Unbelievable. It's a tie!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:41.880
This event is unprecedented in the entire history of PriPara!

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.970
A tie-pri?

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.550
Can that even happen?

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.310
A draw is the last thing I expected.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:52.520
<i>Jigo.</i> Or a draw, as they say.
Profoundly strange and unexpected.

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:55.730
Whaaat?! A draw?!

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.490
Good job-pri.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.320
Let's get snapping!

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:06.070
Yeah!

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:06.990
Here goes!

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:07.750
Allow me!

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.960
Shion? No way!

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:18.130
Shion! What are you doing-pri!?

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:21.850
To play to a draw against me...
I have great expectations of you.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:26.970
Friend Ticket trade! But I'll win the next one. Don't forget that.

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:30.480
Goodbye.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:33.350
That's like a challenge letter or something.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:34.890
Pri?

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:08.780
Manaka! You've been going to PriPara, haven't you?

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:10.530
Eh? Err, err, um...

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:14.780
Don't play dumb! This time I <i>will</i> find hard evidence against you.

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:16.790
I've got an expert on your case.

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:18.750
An expert? Who's that?

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:20.580
A spy or something?

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:23.590
Hmm? Are spies called spies because they like spicy stuff?

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:28.220
Yes, spies actually love— Who cares about that?! I hope you're ready!

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:32.620
Next time: Exclusive Scoop! Lala's Secret Revealed!?

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:34.930
Go for it! Let's go! PriPara!
